This lab runs and depends on third-party software. Nothing below is
redistributed in this repository — Docker pulls the images and pip/Ollama
fetch the rest at setup time — but these are what you end up running.

Container images
  nginx                     BSD-2-Clause
  axllent/mailpit           MIT
  python:3.12-slim          PSF / Debian
  ollama/ollama (optional)  MIT

Python packages
  FastAPI, uvicorn          MIT / BSD-3-Clause
  PyTorch                   BSD-3-Clause
  transformers, huggingface_hub, modelscan   Apache-2.0
  picklescan                MIT
  py7zr and its codecs      LGPL-2.1 / BSD / public domain

Models
  llama3.2:3b               Meta Llama 3.2 Community License.
                            Pulled by setup.sh for Workshop 1. NOT
                            redistributed here. If you would rather not accept
                            that licence, run ./setup.sh --canned; all seven
                            exercises still score.

  Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507   Apache-2.0.
                            The base for exercise 8's optional appendix, which
                            you build yourself. Chosen over Llama specifically
                            because its licence does not constrain naming or
                            redistribution of derivatives.

picklescan and modelscan are real security products, used here as their authors
intended and defeated only in ways their authors have already fixed. The pinned
old versions exist so you can see the bug; see SECURITY.md.
